<title>USA: ROCKWELL UNIT GETS $1.6 MILLION ORDER.</title>
<headline>ROCKWELL UNIT GETS $1.6 MILLION ORDER.</headline>
<dateline>MILWAUKEE, Wis. 1997-08-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Rockwell International Corp's Rockwell Automation said Tuesday it recieved a $1.6 million order for a coordinated drive system from a unit of Avery Dennison Corp.</p>
<p>The drive system will be used by Avery's Fasson Roll division for its coating and laminating machines in a new converting facility in Gotha, Germany, Rockwell said.</p>
<p>Installation of the new drive system is scheduled for December and is part of a $140 million site development plan to be completed by Fasson by 1999, Rockwell said.</p>
<p>-- ((Reuters Chicago Newsdesk 312-408-8787))</p>
